{"format":"helia-content","version":1,"id":"finite-cardinal-arithmetic-topos","title":{"Inline":[{"Text":"Finite Cardinal Arithmetic in a Topos"}]},"title_text":"Finite Cardinal Arithmetic in a Topos","kind":"note","taxon":null,"url":"finite-cardinal-arithmetic-topos.html","content":{"Block":[{"Group":{"role":"entry","attrs":[["entry","finite-cardinal-arithmetic-topos"],["kind","note"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"In a topos with a natural numbers object "},{"Math":{"src":"(N, z, s)"}},{"Text":", you can define finite cardinals as objects that arise as the pullback along a morphism "},{"Math":{"src":"p : ⊤ -> N"}},{"Text":" of the generic finite cardinal. Write "},{"Math":{"src":"[p]"}},{"Text":" for the cardinal corresponding to "},{"Math":{"src":"p"}},{"Text":"."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"The above characterization is a little obtuse and does warrant some more explanation. One way to make it more concrete is that "},{"Math":{"src":"[z] = ⊥"}},{"Text":" and "},{"Math":{"src":"[s ∘ n] = ⊤ ⊕ [n]"}},{"Text":", and that finite cardinals warrant a nice induction principle. If "},{"Math":{"src":"P"}},{"Text":" is a property expressible in the internal language such that "},{"Math":{"src":"⊥"}},{"Text":" satisfies "},{"Math":{"src":"P"}},{"Text":", and that whenever "},{"Math":{"src":"A"}},{"Text":" satisfies "},{"Math":{"src":"P"}},{"Text":" then "},{"Math":{"src":"⊤ ⊕ A"}},{"Text":" satisfies "},{"Math":{"src":"P"}},{"Text":"; then every finite cardinal satisfies "},{"Math":{"src":"P"}},{"Text":". That is, "},{"Math":{"src":"P"}},{"Text":" forms a "},{"Math":{"src":"(z, s)"}},{"Text":"-closed subobject of "},{"Math":{"src":"N"}},{"Text":" and thus "},{"Math":{"src":"P"}},{"Text":" is all of "},{"Math":{"src":"N"}},{"Text":"."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"My working mental model is in a presheaf topos, where the natural numbers object can be defined explicitly as "},{"Math":{"src":"Delta(bb(N))"}},{"Text":"."}]},{"Transclude":{"id":"constant-presheaf","opts":{"expanded":true,"numbered":true,"title":"Auto","level":null,"section":false}}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"The finite cardinals with respect to "},{"Math":{"src":"Delta(bb(N))"}},{"Text":" can be characterized then as,"}]},{"Math":{"src":"[0] ≔ ⊥"}},{"Math":{"src":"[sans(\"suc\")(n)] ≔ ⊤ ⊕ [n]"}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"These obey nice algebraic properties."}]},{"Math":{"src":"[n m] ≅ [n] × [m]"}},{"Math":{"src":"[n + m] ≅ [n] ⊕ [m]"}},{"Math":{"src":"[n^m] ≅ [m] -> [n]"}}]}}}]}}
